    "notes": "Rate-2 Reed-Solomon requires at least 50% of cells for correct recovery.",
    "code_excerpt": "// ReconstructDataColumnSidecars (reconstruction.go):
func MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct() uint64 {
    // (128 + 1) / 2 = 64 (ceiling division)
    return (params.BeaconConfig().NumberOfColumns + 1) / 2
}

func ReconstructDataColumnSidecars(verifiedRoSidecars []blocks.VerifiedRODataColumn) ([]blocks.VerifiedRODataColumn, error) {
    // Deduplicate by column index
    sidecarByIndex := make(map[uint64]blocks.VerifiedRODataColumn, len(verifiedRoSidecars))
    for _, inVerifiedRoSidecar := range verifiedRoSidecars {
        sidecarByIndex[inVerifiedRoSidecar.Index] = inVerifiedRoSidecar
    }
    sidecarCount := len(sidecarByIndex)
    // CHECK: must have >= MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct unique column indices
    if uint64(sidecarCount) < MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct() {
        return nil, ErrNotEnoughDataColumnSidecars
    }
    // For each blob: kzg.RecoverCellsAndKZGProofs(cellsIndices, cells)
    //   cellsIndices has sidecarCount entries (unique column indices)
    //   cells has sidecarCount entries
    // ...
}

// c-kzg-4844 C library recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs:
// if (num_cells > CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB) { ret = C_KZG_BADARGS; goto out; }
// if (num_cells < CELLS_PER_BLOB) { ret = C_KZG_BADARGS; goto out; }
// where CELLS_PER_BLOB = FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_BLOB/FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL = 4096/64 = 64
// and CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB = 128

// Constants:
// NumberOfColumns = 128 (mainnet and minimal both)
// CellsPerBlob (fieldparams) = 64
// CELLS_PER_BLOB (c-kzg) = 64
// MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct = (128+1)/2 = 64

// Go check: sidecarCount >= 64 (done before C call)
// C check: num_cells >= 64 (inside C library)
// Both thresholds are 64 = exactly 50% of 128

// ReconstructBlobs uses different constant name but same value:
// cellsPerBlob = fieldparams.CellsPerBlob = 64
// if len(verifiedDataColumnSidecars) < cellsPerBlob { return nil, ErrNotEnoughDataColumnSidecars }
// Also requires sorted order and unique indices (checked earlier in function)

// Summary: all three enforcement points (Go-level in ReconstructDataColumnSidecars,
// Go-level in ReconstructBlobs, C-level in recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs) correctly
// enforce >= 64 minimum, which is exactly 50% of 128 total columns"
  },
  {
    "check_id": "W7B8:W7B8:CHK-0130",
    "property_id": "PROP-W5B14-14",
    "title": "Is the 50% threshold correctly derived from CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB constant?",
    "severity": "High",
    "bug_class": "Threshold Derivation Error",
    "notes": "The 50% threshold is a mathematical requirement of rate-2 Reed-Solomon coding.",
    "code_excerpt": "// Threshold derivation analysis:
// CELLS_PER_EXT_BLOB = FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_EXT_BLOB / FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL
//                   = (FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_BLOB << 1) / 64
//                   = (4096 << 1) / 64 = 8192 / 64 = 128
// CELLS_PER_BLOB = FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_BLOB / 64 = 4096/64 = 64
// MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct = (128+1)/2 = 64 (ceiling of 128/2)
// For even NumberOfColumns: ceiling(N/2) = N/2 = 64 ✓ (correct: exactly 50%)
// For odd NumberOfColumns: would be (N+1)/2 which is 1 more than floor(N/2)

// The formula (N+1)/2 is technically ceiling division
// For N=128 (even): (128+1)/2 = 64 (integer division, since 129/2=64 in Go int)
// This is exactly 50% = 64 out of 128. CORRECT.

// Spec reference: Reed-Solomon rate-2 code: k=64 data cells, n=128 extended cells
// Minimum cells required for interpolation = k = 64 (any 64 of the 128 cells)

// Potential off-by-one concern:
// Is >= 64 correct or should it be > 64?
// Rate-2 RS erasure code: you need EXACTLY k data symbols (64) to reconstruct
// With any 64 out of 128, you can recover the polynomial uniquely
// The check is: sidecarCount >= MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct() = >= 64
// This means 64 is ACCEPTED, 63 is REJECTED. This is CORRECT.

// Integer overflow concern:
// params.BeaconConfig().NumberOfColumns is uint64
// (NumberOfColumns + 1) would overflow if NumberOfColumns = ^uint64(0)
// But NumberOfColumns is always 128 per spec, bounded by SSZ constraints
// In practice: no overflow risk for valid beacon configs

// Consistency check:
// fieldparams.CellsPerBlob = 64 (compile-time constant)
// params.BeaconConfig().NumberOfColumns = 128 (runtime parameter, but same value)
// MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct uses runtime NumberOfColumns
// ReconstructBlobs uses compile-time CellsPerBlob = 64
// These must stay synchronized. If NumberOfColumns ever changes (it won't for mainnet),
// MinimumColumnCountToReconstruct would change but ReconstructBlobs would not.
// This is a latent consistency issue but not a current vulnerability.

// Recovery shortcut in ReconstructBlobs:
// if verifiedDataColumnSidecars[cellsPerBlob-1].Index == uint64(cellsPerBlob-1)
//    i.e., if the 64th sidecar has column index 63 (the first 64 columns present)
// Then skip reconstruction by using blobSidecarsFromDataColumnSidecars directly
// This requires exactly columns 0..63 (the 'original' half of the erasure code)
// This is a valid optimization: if you have the original 64 data cells (columns 0..63),
// you don't need to run erasure decoding at all.
// The check verifiedDataColumnSidecars[63].Index == 63 ensures the SORTED last element
// of the first 64 is index 63, which confirms 0..63 are present (due to sort+unique earlier)"
  }
]

